Package c's only assembly file is a symbolic link to a file outside every package,
which go/build lists among c's files as it lists a regular one, so c holds a non-Go
source and every declaration of it is retained. Package e holds a symbolic link
named like an assembly file that points at a directory, which go/build skips, so
e holds none and its variable is not retained. The linked file names nothing but
c's own function.

-- go.mod --
module example.com/linked

go 1.27.0
-- shared/impl.s --
TEXT ·run(SB), $0
	RET
-- c/c.go --
package c

var size int

func run()
-- c/run_amd64.s.symlink --
../shared/impl.s
-- e/e.go --
package e

var spare int
-- e/dir.s.symlink --
../shared
-- main.go --
package main

import (
	_ "example.com/linked/c"
	_ "example.com/linked/e"
)

func main() {}
